<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">

  <PropertyGroup>
    <TargetFrameworks>net8.0;net10.0</TargetFrameworks>
    <ImplicitUsings>enable</ImplicitUsings>
    <Nullable>enable</Nullable>
    <LangVersion>latest</LangVersion>

    <!-- NuGet Package Metadata -->
    <PackageId>Sendspin.SDK</PackageId>
    <Version>9.3.3</Version>
    <Authors>Sendspin Contributors</Authors>
    <Company>Sendspin</Company>
    <Product>Sendspin SDK</Product>
    <Description>Cross-platform SDK for the Sendspin synchronized multi-room audio protocol. Connect to Music Assistant servers and play synchronized audio across multiple devices.</Description>
    <PackageTags>sendspin;audio;multiroom;sync;music-assistant;streaming</PackageTags>
    <PackageProjectUrl>https://github.com/Sendspin/sendspin-dotnet</PackageProjectUrl>
    <RepositoryUrl>https://github.com/Sendspin/sendspin-dotnet</RepositoryUrl>
    <RepositoryType>git</RepositoryType>
    <PackageLicenseExpression>MIT</PackageLicenseExpression>
    <PackageReadmeFile>README.md</PackageReadmeFile>
    <PackageReleaseNotes>
v9.3.3 - Playback timing (9.x legacy line):

Two fixes. No API removals; one new option, one new capability, one new event.

- A stream that restarts late no longer stays late. The startup sync-error
  baseline exists to absorb an output backend's first fill, and it was bounded
  only by the 500 ms re-anchor threshold: a restart that landed half a second
  late inside the re-anchor cooldown was absorbed as a "constant offset that
  will not be corrected", and the stream played half a second late at a
  reported error of zero for its whole duration (chrisuthe/windowsSpin#63).
  The baseline is now bounded by
  SyncCorrectionOptions.StartupBaselineAllowanceMicroseconds (150 ms); past
  that the error stays visible and the one-shot snap tier closes it.
- Live sources no longer cut out. A source role delivers audio in real time
  from its first chunk, and the server schedules that chunk only min_buffer_ms
  ahead; the buffer pre-rolls playback by the host's output latency, so a
  WASAPI host's 100 ms prefill left about 50 ms of the default 150 ms for the
  network and the decoder. required_lead_time_ms and min_buffer_ms are now
  reported with the output latency added, from the initial client/state on:
  ClientCapabilities.ExpectedOutputLatencyMs until a player has measured one,
  the measured value after, re-reported through the new
  IAudioPipeline.OutputLatencyChanged event only when the numbers move. Hosts
  that had folded their backend's latency into RequiredLeadTimeMs or
  MinBufferMs themselves should stop, or it is counted twice; WASAPI hosts
  should set ExpectedOutputLatencyMs to their buffer size (typically 100 ms).

----

      Earlier release notes: https://github.com/Sendspin/sendspin-dotnet/releases
    </PackageReleaseNotes>
    <Copyright>Copyright © 2024-2026 Sendspin Contributors</Copyright>

    <!-- Enable source link for debugging -->
    <PublishRepositoryUrl>true</PublishRepositoryUrl>
    <EmbedUntrackedSources>true</EmbedUntrackedSources>
    <IncludeSymbols>true</IncludeSymbols>
    <SymbolPackageFormat>snupkg</SymbolPackageFormat>

    <!-- Generate XML documentation -->
    <GenerateDocumentationFile>true</GenerateDocumentationFile>
    <NoWarn>$(NoWarn);CS1591</NoWarn>

    <!-- NativeAOT and trimming compatibility -->
    <IsAotCompatible>true</IsAotCompatible>
    <IsTrimmable>true</IsTrimmable>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <InternalsVisibleTo Include="Sendspin.SDK.Tests" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <!-- Core dependencies - all cross-platform -->
    <PackageReference Include="Concentus" Version="2.2.2" />
    <PackageReference Include="Zeroconf" Version="3.7.16" />
    <PackageReference Include="Makaretu.Dns.Multicast" Version="0.27.0" />
    <PackageReference Include="System.Text.Json" Version="8.0.5" />
    <PackageReference Include="Microsoft.Extensions.Logging.Abstractions" Version="8.0.2" />
    <PackageReference Include="Microsoft.SourceLink.GitHub" Version="8.0.0" PrivateAssets="All" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <None Include="README.md" Pack="true" PackagePath="\" />
  </ItemGroup>

</Project>
